    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92945" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥωπο-γράφος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γρᾰ],
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥῶπος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one that
				paints petty subjects</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥῶπες</span>, glossed as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕλη καὶ
				ὑλώδη φυτά</span>), such as <i>still life</i>,
				like the Dutch masters, <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				705.55
			</span></i>, perh. to be read in Donat.ad Ter.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Eun.</u>
				253
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥυπαρογράφος</span>.</div>
